hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5281","Muhammad bin Mansour al-Tusi told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told me, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No Breastfeeding is forbidden by either sucking or sucking. Rather, it is forbidden to express milk.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5282","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “My uncle Aflah asked permission for me after the veil was removed, but I did not give him permission, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him, He said: Permit me to him, for he is your uncle. I said: O Messenger of God, the woman breastfed me, but the man did not breastfeed me. He said: Permit me to breastfeed him. May your right hand be touched, for he is your uncle.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5283","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ibn Juraij informed us, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Urwa, Aisha told him, she said: “My uncle Abu al-Ja’d came from breastfeeding, so I brought him back. He said: Hisham said: He is Abu al-Qu’ais. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and I informed him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give me permission to him.”"
"5284","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, that Aisha told her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with her, and that she heard the voice of a man asking permission in Hafsa’s house. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, “This is a man asking permission to enter your house.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I see him as so-and-so. To Hafsa’s paternal uncle through breastfeeding. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, if so-and-so were alive, her maternal paternal uncle would enter upon me, so the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Breastfeeding forbids what childbirth forbids."
"5285","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told us, he said: My father told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, “The brother of Abu al-Qu’ais” asked permission to come to Aisha after the verse about the hijab, but she refused to give him permission. This was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Allow me to go to him, for he is your uncle. I said: The woman breastfed me and he did not breastfeed me. The man said: He is your uncle, so let him visit you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5286","Harun bin Abdullah told us, Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “Aflah, the brother of Abu al-Qu’ais, came to ask permission for me, and he is blind through breastfeeding, so I refused to give him permission, until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came.” May God bless him and grant him peace. So I told him, and he said: Allow me to go to him, for he is your uncle. Aisha said: That was after the veil was revealed."
"5287","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Aswad and Ishaq bin Bakr told us, they said: Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Jafar Ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of Arak Ibn Malik, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Aflah, the brother of Abi al-Qu’ais, came to ask for permission, and I said: No.” I gave him permission until he asked permission from the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, I said to him: Aflah, my father’s brother, has come. Al-Qu'ais asked for permission, but I refused to give him permission. So he said: Allow me to give him permission, for he is your uncle. I said: The wife of Abu Al-Qu'ais breastfed me and he did not The man is breastfeeding me. He said: Give him permission, for he is your uncle.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5288","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning Ibn Uyaynah, he said: We heard it from Abdul Al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Sahila bint Suhail came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I see in Abu Hudhayfah faced Salim when Ali entered and said: Then breastfeed him. She said: How can I breastfeed him when he is an old man? He said: Don’t I know that he is a man? Then she came after, and said: By the One who sent you with the truth as a prophet, I have never seen anything in Abu Hudhayfah’s face yet that I hate.” Sufyan al-Thawri disagreed with him, So he sent the hadith. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, meaning Ibn Mahdi, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning the revolutionary, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “said to Sahla: Breastfeed him. She said: He is a man,” so the hadith was invalid. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5289","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ Sahlah came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, “Salim is entering upon us, and he has reasoned as men do.” And he knew what men knew. He said: Breastfeed him and you will become a mahram for him with that. So I stayed for a while not speaking about it, and I met Al-Qasim, and he said: Tell him about it and do not You fear him"
"5290","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb informed us, he said: Yunus, who is the son of Yazid, and Malik informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, said: “All the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, refused to let any of the people enter upon them with that breastfeeding.” He wanted to breastfeed the elder, and they said to Aisha: By God, we do not see that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded Sahlah bint Suhail except a concession in Salem was breastfed alone by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. By God, no one will enter upon us with this breastfeeding, nor will he see us.” Aqeel disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5291","Abdul Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Uqail told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah bin Zam’a told me that his mother Zainab bint Abi Salamah told him that her mother Umm Salamah’s wife The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: “All of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, refused for anyone to enter upon them with that breastfeeding. They said to Aisha: By God, we see this as nothing but a concession granted by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, specifically to Salem, so no one should enter upon us. With this breastfeeding, and he does not see us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5292","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Makhramah bin Bukayr told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Humaid bin Nafi’ said: I heard Zainab bint Abi Salamah saying: I heard Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “She came Sahla bint Suhail went to the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: O Messenger of God, “I see on the face of Abu Hudhayfah the sign of Salem’s entry Ali. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Breastfeed him. I said: He has a beard. He said: Breastfeed him. What is on my father’s face will go away. Hudhayfah, she said: By God, I did not recognize him in the face of Abu Hudhayfah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5293","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir told us, he said: I heard Ibn Wahb, he said: Sulayman told me, on the authority of Yahya, and Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Qasim On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Sahlah, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah, to breastfeed Salim, Abu Hudhayfah’s servant, until Abu Hudhayfah’s jealousy went away, so she breastfed him while he was a man.” Rabi’ah said: So it was a concession for Salem. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5294","Amr bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, he said: Ayoub informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, “ Salim, Abu Hudhayfah’s client, was with Abu Hudhayfah and his family in their house, so Bint Suhail came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “Indeed, Salim has reached what the men have reached, and has understood what they have understood, and he is entering upon us, and I suspect that Abu Hudhayfah is in his heart because of that.” Something, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Breastfeed him, so that you may become a mahram for him. So she breastfed him, and what was in Abu Hudhayfah’s soul was gone.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5295","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Hajjaj, on the authority of his father, said: I said: O Messenger of God, “What will remove from me the blame of breastfeeding?” He said: “Ghurrah”: a male or female slave. Sufyan disagreed with him. Bin Saeed"
"5296","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Kawsaj Al-Maruzi told us, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hajjaj Al-Aslami, said: I said: O Messenger of God, “What will remove from me the blame of breastfeeding?” He said: Ghurrah: a slave. \or a nation\"""""
"5297","Ali ibn Hajar al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Ismail, meaning Ibn Ulayya, informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, he said: Ubaid bin Abi Maryam told me, on the authority of Uqba bin Al-Harith, he said: I heard it from Uqba, but I have memorized the hadith of Ubaid. He said: “ I married a woman, and a black woman came to us and said: I have breastfed you both. So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, So I said: I married so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so, then a black woman came to me and said: I have breastfed you both, so he turned away from me, so I went to him from Before his face, I said: She is a liar. He said: So what about her when she claimed that she had breastfed you both? Leave her alone. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5298","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed and Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Aswad, On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Judama bint Wahb told her that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I was about to He forbade adultery, to the point that I mentioned that Persia and the Romans do it.” And Ishaq said: They do it, so it does not harm their children."
"5299","Ismail bin Masoud and Humayd bin Masada told us, saying: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurayi, he said: Ibn Awn told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Bishr bin Masoud al-Ansari, and he narrated the hadith until he referred it to Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, he said: It was mentioned before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “And what is that? We said: A man has a breastfeeding woman, and he gets infected from her. He would not like her to become pregnant by him, and he would have a slave girl, so he would have sexual intercourse with her, and he would not like her to become pregnant by him. He said: No, you should not do that. For it is destiny.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5300","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Fayd, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Murrah al-Zarqi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Zarqi said that a man asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about isolation, and he said: My wife is breastfeeding, and I hate for her to become pregnant. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, what has been decreed in the womb will come to pass.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5301","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: He is Ibn Salih, Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Al-Baraa, said: “I met my uncle and he had the flag, so I said: Where are you going? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to A man who marries his father’s wife after him: I behead him or kill him.” Narrated by Zayd bin Abi Unaisa, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, On the authority of Yazid bin Al-Baraa"
"5302","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Jaafar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah is the son of Amr Al-Ruqi, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Baraa, on the authority of his father, said: I met my uncle and he had a flag, so I said: “Where do you want?” The Messenger of God sent me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to a man who had had intercourse with his father’s wife, so he ordered me to behead him and take his money.”"
"5303","Muhammad bin Qudamah Al-Masisi told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, who is Ibn Tarif, on the authority of Abu Al-Jahm, on the authority of Al-Baraa, he said: “ During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I was going around those neighborhoods on my camels, when I saw horsemen and horsemen with a banner, so he made The Bedouins were seeking refuge with me, due to my position with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so they came to us, and they went around a dome and brought out a man. So they beheaded him, and they did not ask him about anything. So I asked about his story, and they said: They found him having married his father’s wife, and then they left. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5304","5344 Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Rahawi told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan is Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Uthman Al-Batti, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, said: “We captured captives on the day of Awtas, and they had wives, so we hated to attack them. So we asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was revealed: And chaste women, except those your right hands possess. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5305","Muhammad bin Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, whose name is Saleh, on the authority of Abu Alqamah Al-Hashimi, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent An army to Awtas, and they met an enemy, and they fought them and defeated them, and they captured captives of theirs who had wives among the polytheists, and it was Muslims are embarrassed by their deceit, so God Almighty revealed: And the chaste women, except those whom your right hands possess, that is, this is lawful for you. “When their waiting period has expired.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5306","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Ulayyah informed us, saying: Ishaq is the son of Yusuf al-Azraq, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar. On the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the use of shughar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5307","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: I am Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace “He forbade shughar”"
"5308","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “There is no ugliness, no impurity, and no shigra in Islam, and whoever plunders is not one of us.”"
"5309","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Al-Fazari, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “No turmoil, no impurity, and no shughar.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is wrong, and the one before it is correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5310","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’. H and Al-Harith bin Miskin, a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik, Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade shughar,” and shughar: for a man to give another man his daughter in marriage, provided that he gives him his daughter in marriage, and not between them. Friendship"
"5311","Muhammad bin Ibrahim and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Ishaq al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, On the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade Al-Shughar.” Ubayd Allah said: And Al-Shughar: The man was He marries his daughter on the condition that he gives him his sister in marriage (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5312","Qutaibah told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Suhayb, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, Qutaibah told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, and Shuaib, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “emancipated Safiya, and made him her friend.”"
"5313","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Sufyan told us, and Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn al-Hubhab, on the authority of Anas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, freed Safiyyah. And he made freeing her her dowry.” And the wording refers to Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5314","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Zubayd, Abtar bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Burdah, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever frees his female slave and then marries her will have two rewards.”"
"5315","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, he said: Saleh bin Saleh told me, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Three people will be given their reward twice: A man who had a female slave, and he trained her and taught her well.” He taught her and taught her well, then he freed her and married her. He is a servant who fulfills the rights of God and the rights of his master, and a believer of the People of the Book.”"
"5316","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar informed us, saying: Ja`far ibn Sulaiman informed us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “Abu Talha proposed to Umm Salim, so she said: By God, there is no one like you, Abu Talha, who would be rejected, but you are an infidel man, and I am a Muslim woman, and it is not permissible for me to I will marry you. If you submit, then that is my dowry. I do not ask you for anything else. If you submit, then that is her dowry.” Thabit said: “So I did not hear.” Never with a woman who had a more generous dowry than the mother of Sulaym al-Islam, so he consummated the marriage with her and she bore him a son. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5317","Qutaibah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, he said: “He married Abu Talha, Umm Sulaim, and the friendship between them was Islam. Umm Sulaim converted to Islam before Abu Talha, so he proposed to her, and she said: I have “I became a Muslim, so if you convert to Islam, I will marry you and he will convert to Islam, and it will be the friendship between them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5318","Qutaibah told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa’d, “that a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted her, and she said: O Messenger of God, “I have come to give myself to you.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at her and looked up at her. He corrected it, then lowered his head. When the woman saw that he had not made any decision on her, she sat down, then a man from his companions stood up and said: Yes. Messenger of God, if you do not have a need for her, then marry her to me. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No, by God, I did not find anything. He said: Look, even an iron ring. So he went and came back and said: No, by God, O Messenger of God, nor An iron ring, but this is my garment. Sahl said: If he has a robe, she gets half of it. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What are you doing? With your garment? If she wears it, she will not have any of it on her, and if she wears it, she will not have any of it on her. So the man sat until he sat for a long time, then he got up. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him as a servant, so he ordered him to be summoned, and when he came, he said: What do you have of the Qur’an? He said: I have such-and-such Surah, and such-and-such Surah. He enumerated them, and said: Do you recite them by heart? He said: Yes. He said: I made her king based on what you know of the Qur’an."
"5319","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Bahili, on the authority of Asal bin Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, a woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and presented She wanted herself, so he said to her: Sit. She sat for an hour, and he said: Sit, may God bless you. As for us, we have no need of you, but you have control over me. Your command? She said: Yes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at the faces of the people and called a man from them and said: I want to marry this woman to you. If you are satisfied, he said: You have not satisfied me, O Messenger of God, I have been satisfied. Then he said to the man: Do you have anything? He said: No, by God. He said: Go to the women. He went to them, but did not find anything with them. He said: What of the Qur’an have you memorized? He said: Surah Al-Baqarah, or the one that follows it. He said: Then stand up and teach her twenty verses, and she is your wife."
"5320","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz bin Suhaib told us, he said: I heard Anas say: Abd al-Rahman bin Awf said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw me at the wedding screen, so I said: I got married.” An Ansar woman. He said: How much did you give her in charity? He said: The weight of a stone of gold."
"5321","Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Masry and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading from him while I was listening, and the wording is Muhammad’s, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, On the authority of Malik, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf” came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with him Athar Al-Safra, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked him and told him that he had married a woman from the Ansar, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: How much did you drive to it? He said: An adulterous weight of a stone of gold. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have a family, even if it is a sheep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5322","Hilal bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Amr bin Shuaib told me, and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim, he said: I heard Hajjaj, saying: Ibn Jurayj said, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Any woman who is married to a dowry, a lover, or an iddah before the infallibility of the marriage, then it is hers, and whatever comes after it.” A protection, so it belongs to the one who gave it to him, and the most worthy of what a man has been honored with is his daughter or his sister.” The wording is by Abdullah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5323","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told us, on the authority of Musa bin Left, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “The dowry, when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was among us, was ten uqs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5324","Ali ibn Hajar ibn Iyas ibn Muqatil ibn Mushmurj ibn Khalid informed us, saying: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub and Ibn Aoun, Salama bin Alqamah, and Hisham bin Hassan, the hadiths of one of them were included in each other, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Salama, on the authority of Ibn Sirin: I was informed on the authority of Abu Al-Ajafa, and others said on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abu Al-Ajafa, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab said: “Don’t you go to extremes.” Be honest with women, for if it were an honor in this world or piety in the sight of God Almighty, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would have been worthy of it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave in charity to any of his wives, and none of his daughters gave in charity more than twelve uqiyahs, and that A man will become jealous of his wife’s charity until he creates enmity towards her towards him, and until he says: I entrusted you with the waterskin, and I was an Arab boy. I was born, but I did not know what attached to the waterskin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5325","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad Al-Duri told us, he said: Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married her while she was on the land of Abyssinian, the Negus married her off, gave her four thousand foals, prepared them from him, and sent them with Sharhabeel ibn Hasanah, and he did not The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would send something to her, and the dowry for his wives was four hundred dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5326","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Had, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, said: I asked Aisha about that, and she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid for twelve uqiyahs.” Wanash, and that is five hundred dirhams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5327","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala and Sulayman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: He told me Urwah bin Al-Zubair, that he asked Aisha “about the words of God Almighty: And if you fear that you will not be just towards the orphans, then marry what pleases you.” Of the women, she said: O son of my sister, she is an orphan who is in the custody of her guardian, sharing with him his wealth, and he admires her wealth and her beauty. Her guardian wants to marry her without being fair in her friendship, so he gives her the same as what he gives to someone else, so they are forbidden from marrying them unless That they should be fair to them, and that they should reach their highest age in terms of dowry, so they were commanded to marry whatever women pleased them besides themselves, Urwah said. Aisha said: Then the people consulted the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about them, so God Almighty revealed: And they ask you for a question concerning Women: Say, “May God give you a fatwa concerning them,” to His saying: “And you desire to marry them.” Aisha said: “And what God Almighty has mentioned should be recited.” In the Book is the first verse in which it says: And if you fear that you will not do justice to orphans, then marry such women as please you. Aisha said: And the saying God in the other verse: And you desire to marry them, as one of you desires for his orphan who is in his custody, when she is short of money. And camels, they were forbidden from marrying orphan women whom they desired for their money, except with justice, because of their desire on their behalf.”"
"5328","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Abu Sa`id Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Zaida bin Qudamah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and Al-Aswad, said: “Abdullah was brought about a man who married a woman and did not impose He died before he entered it, so Abdullah said: “Ask, do you find any traces of it?” They said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, we do not find anything in it, meaning: a trace. He said: I say in my opinion, and if it is correct, then it is from God. She gets it as a dowry. Her wives, no sexual intercourse or negligence, she has the inheritance, and she must observe the waiting period. Then a man of the bravest of men stood up and said: In a case like this, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling. May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding a woman called Baru’ bint Washiq. She married a man and he died before consummating the sexual intercourse with her, so he decided for her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is like the dowry of her wives, and she is entitled to the inheritance, and she is required to observe the waiting period.” So Abdullah raised his hands and said “Allahu Akbar.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know anyone. He said in this hadith: Black, without an additional (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5329","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abd God said, “Indeed, he came concerning a woman whom a man had married, and he died, and he had not imposed a dowry on her, nor had he consummated the sexual intercourse with her. So they went to him, close to him.” A month without giving them a fatwa. Then, he said: I see that she will have the dowry of her wives, no sexual intercourse or excess, and she will have the inheritance and she will have to wait for the waiting period. Ma’qil bin testified. Sinan Al-Ashja’i, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling regarding Barwa’ bint Washiq in the same manner as what you judged.” And on the authority of Ishaq bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Mu'tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Mansour, with it"
"5330","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, “Concerning a man who married a woman, and she died without consummating the sexual intercourse with her, and he did not fulfill the obligation for her. He said: She is entitled to the dowry, and she is required to observe the waiting period, and she is entitled to The inheritance, and Maqil bin Sinan said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decree it in the case of Baru’ bint Washiq. “Ishaq bin Mansour, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, similar to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5331","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ali bin Mushar told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah A people came to him and said: “A man from among us married a woman, and he did not impose a dowry on her, nor did he bring her together until he died.” So he said: Abdullah: I have not been asked since I left the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, something more difficult for me than this. So they came to someone else and differed with him therein for a month. Then they said to him at the end of that: Who do we ask if we do not ask you, and you are among the greatest companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this country, and no Can we find someone else? He said: I will express my opinion on it, and if it is correct, then it is from God alone, with no partner, and if it is wrong, then from me and from whom? Satan, and God and His Messenger are free from him, I think I should give her the dowry of her wives, no deception or excess, and she will have the inheritance, and it is her duty. The period is four months and ten. He said: That was because people from Ashjaa heard it, so they stood up and said: We bear witness that you have decreed what the Messenger of God decreed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him regarding a woman from among us who is called Baru’ bint Washiq. He said: Abdullah was not seen rejoicing over that day except “By his Islam” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5332","Shuaib bin Yusuf al-Nasa’i told us, on the authority of Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Ashja’i, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud was very happy, and a man came to him and asked him, “About a man who gave his daughter to a man, and she died before he could have consummated the marriage with her.” He said, “And he did not do so.” She has the dowry, and he said: She has the full dowry, she has to pay the waiting period, and she has the inheritance. Maqil bin Sinan said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He decreed it in Baru’ bint Washiq.” Al-Ashja’i said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decree it and he was so happy he had never been more happy. He told us. Muhammad bin Bashar, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning dandy, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: Abdullah was asked about a woman who died. On the authority of her husband, he reminded him of what he said: Then a man from Ashjaa stood up and said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed a ruling regarding us in a similar manner.” This is about a woman from among us called Roua’ bint Washiq. Ibn Masoud said: Is there anyone with you? Some of them stood up and testified. He told us. Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam Al-Basri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It differed to Abdullah spent a month on the account of a man who had died and had not imposed a dowry on his wife, so he mentioned it, and in it: Maqil ibn Sinan stood up and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a judgement. May God bless him and grant him peace, in Baru’a bint Washiq like this, Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahawi informed us, on the authority of Ya’la, who is Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ismail is Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Amer, meaning Ash-Sha’abi, who said: Ibn Masoud was brought about a woman whose husband died, and he did not fulfill the religious duties for her. He narrated the hadith, saying: Maqil bin Sinan said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling regarding Barwa’ bint Washiq like this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5333","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “A woman came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I have given myself to you.” She stood for a long time, and he stood up. A man, and he said: Marry her to me if you have no need for her. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you have anything? He said: My garment. Then he, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If you give it to him, you will sit without your garment on, so look for something. He said: I cannot find anything. He said: Look for even a ring from He searched for iron and did not find anything. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Do you have anything of the Qur’an? He said: Yes, Surah such-and-such. And such-and-such surah refers to the surah he named. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have married her to you based on what you know of the Qur’an.”"
"5334","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I heard Abu Hazim, saying: I heard Sahl bin Saad, saying: I am in The people were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and a woman stood up and said: O Messenger of God, she has given herself to you, so flee for her. What do you think? She remained silent, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not answer her with anything. Then she got up and said: She has given herself to you, so he fled. In your opinion, a man stood up and said: Marry her, O Messenger of God. He said: Do you have anything? He said: No. He said: Go and ask for something. So he went and asked, then came and said: O Messenger of God, I did not find anything. He said: Go and ask, even if it is an iron ring. So he went and asked and then He came and said: I did not find anything, not even an iron ring. He said: Do you have anything of the Qur’an? He said: Yes, I have Surah such-and-such and Surah such-and-such. He said: You have married her based on what you know of the Qur’an.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5335","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: Ya’qub told us, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, that A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, “I have come to devote myself to you.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, looked at her. May God bless him and grant him peace. He looked up at her and looked straight at her, then lowered his head. When the woman saw that he had not made up her mind anything, she sat down. Then a man from one of his companions stood up and said: Yes, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if you do not have a need for her, then marry her to me. He said: Do you have any need for her? Do you have anything? He said: No, by God, I did not find anything. He said: Look, even an iron ring. He went away and came back, and said: No, by God, O Messenger. By God, nor an iron ring, but this is my garment. Sahl said: It has no robe. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What are you doing? With your garment? If you wear it, you will not have any of it on her, and if you wear it, you will not have any of it on you. So the man sat for a long time. Then he got up and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him as a servant, so he ordered him to be summoned, and when he came, he said: What do you have of the Qur’an? He said: I have a surah He enumerated them such-and-such and such-and-such Surahs. He said: Do you recite them by heart? He said: Yes. He said: I have given them control over them based on what you have of the Qur’an."
"5336","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abtar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught us the tashahhud in prayer, and the tashahhud in a need. He said: The tashahhud in a need: that praise be to God. We seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of our own souls. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. And I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and he recites three verses: “Shu’bah ibn al-Hajjaj disagreed with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5337","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Teach them the needful sermon: Praise be to God. We seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Him.” By God from the evils of our own souls. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that there is no god but God. That Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then three verses are recited: O you who have believed, fear Allah as He deserves to fear Him, and do not die except as Muslims. O people, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from them many men and women. Those who believe fear God and speak words of righteousness. Then He will remember his need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5338","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Muhammad bin Issa told us, he said: Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Dawud On the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man spoke to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about something, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, May God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, praise be to God, we praise Him and seek His help. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. And I bear witness.” “There is no god but God alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, as for what follows.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5339","Ishaq bin Mansour Al-Maruzi informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, informed us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, informed us, On the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim bin Tarfa, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: “Two men bore witness before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. One of them said: Whoever obeys God and His Messenger has guided him, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wretched. \You are the fiancé\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5340","Issa bin Hammad bin Zaghbah informed us, saying: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amer, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most deserving of conditions is that you fulfill in fulfillment what you have made private sexual intercourse permissible.”"
"5341","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told us, saying: I heard Hajjaj, who is the one-eyed son of Muhammad, saying: Ibn Juraij said, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any woman who is married to A dowry, or a lover, or a waiting period before the inviolability of marriage is hers, and whatever comes after the infallibility of the marriage is for the one to whom it was given. “The most deserving thing for which a man is honored is his daughter or his sister.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5342","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim Al-Masisi told us, saying: I heard Hajjaj, saying: Ibn Juraij said: Saeed bin Abi Ayoub told me, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Abu Al-Khair narrated to him, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, he is more deserving of Conditions: That you give in return what you have made lawful for private parts.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5343","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She came Rifa'ah's wife went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: \Rif'ah divorced me"
"5344","Ali bin Hajar Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Jafar, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, established Peace be upon him, he passed between Khaybar and Medina three times, building with Safiyya bint Huyay. So I invited the Muslims to a feast, but there was no bread or food in it. Meat, and he was ordered to feed her, so dates, aqat, and ghee were thrown at her, and that was his feast. The Muslims said: One of the mothers of Believers or from among those whose right hand possesses? So he said: If he veils her, then she is one of the mothers of the believers, and if he does not veil her, then she is among those whose right hand possesses. Then, when he traveled, he stepped on his back for her and stretched the veil between her and the people.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5345","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzail, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, cursed the woman who tattooed him and the woman who was tattooed, the one who connects her and the woman connected to her, the one who consumes usury and his one who pays it, and the one who allows it.” And the one for whom it is permissible”"
"5346","Bishr bin Khaled Al-Askari told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he is Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Once, on the authority of Al-Harith Al-Awar, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The one who consumes usury and its one who pays it, and its witnesses and its scribes, when they know, and the one who betrays it.” And the one who seeks beauty, and the one who commits charity, will be cursed according to the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, until the Day of Resurrection.” The analyst did not mention And what is permissible for him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5347","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Asim told us, meaning the noble, he said: Zakaria bin Ishaq told us, he said: I am Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “We used to do it, meaning the pleasure of women, during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the time of Abu Bakr, and Sadr From the caliphate of Omar until Omar forbade us from it. “Shu’bah disagreed with him.”"
"5348","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I heard Al-Hasan bin Muhammad narrating On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah and Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, they said: “The caller of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out and said: God has given you permission. So have fun""
5349""","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muslim Al-Quray, he said: We entered upon the names Daughter of Abu Bakr, so we asked her “about sexual intercourse with women,” and she said: “We did it during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5349",""
"5350","Ahmed bin Uthman bin Hakim told me, he said: Khalid bin Mukhlid told me, he said: Suleiman bin Bilal told me, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz told me, he said: A man from Banu Sabra told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says, “In the Farewell Pilgrimage: God has forbidden Mut’ah, so do not approach it. He wants Mut’ah for women, and whoever is in need of any of it.” Let him leave it.”"
"5351","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar. On the authority of Rabi’, who is Ibn Sabra, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He made a concession in mut’a, so a man spoke to a woman, and when he After that, I heard him forbidding it in the strongest terms, and saying the strongest words about it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5352","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Basri told me, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abd Rabbuh ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sabrah, on the authority of his father, who is called Al-Sabri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. That: “He ordered them to have sexual intercourse, so a man and I got engaged to a woman, so I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, after three days, and behold, he was making her forbidden.” It is strictly forbidden, and it is strictly forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5353","Mughirah bin Abdul Rahman Al-Harrani told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Maqil told us, and he is Ibn Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Abla, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, said: Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra told me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “forbade Concerning Mut’ah, he said: “It is forbidden from this day of yours until the Day of Resurrection, and whoever is given something should not take it back.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5354","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Wahb bin Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Ubayy told us, he said: I heard Ibn Ishaq narrating, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade Mut’ah on the day of \conquest\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5355","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sabra. On the authority of his father, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In the year of the conquest, he forbade women’s sexual intercourse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5356","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, meaning Al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Umar, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, And Abdullah, the son of Muhammad, on the authority of their father, that Ali had heard that a man saw no harm in pleasure, so he said: You are lost. The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace on her behalf, and on the meat of domestic donkeys on the Day of Khaybar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5357","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us. It was recited to him while I was listening, and the pronunciation is Muhammad’s. He said: Ibn al-Qasim informed us. On the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah, and Al-Hasan, the sons of Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of their father, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade women’s sexual intercourse on the Day of Khaybar, and the meat of female donkeys.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5358","Amr bin Ali, Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, they said: Abdul-Wahhab is Al-Thaqafi told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari, says: Malik bin Anas told me that Ibn Shihab told him that Abdullah and Al-Hasan are the sons of Muhammad bin Ali told him that their father, Muhammad bin Ali, told them that Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And peace be upon him on the day of the news of women’s sexual intercourse.” Ibn al-Muthanna said: the day of Hunayn, and he said: This is what Abd al-Wahhab told us from his book. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5359","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sabrah Al-Juhani, on the authority of his father, that he said: The Messenger of God gave permission May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and I and a man went to a woman from Bani Amir, and we introduced ourselves to her, and she said: What will you give me? So I said: My robe, and my friend said: My robe, and my friend’s robe was better than mine, and I was younger than him, so if you look at the robe My friend liked her, and when she looked at me, she liked her, and she said: You and your robe are enough for me. So I stayed with her for three days, and then the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever has any of these women whom he enjoys, let him let her go.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This Authentic hadith"
"5360","Muhammad ibn Bashhar told us, he said: Muhammad told me, meaning Ghandar, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Khaled ibn Arfatah, On the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said about a man who has intercourse with his wife’s concubine. He said: “If If it is permissible for him, I will flog him for a hundred, and if it is not permissible for him, I will stone him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5361","Yaqoub bin Mahan Al-Baghdadi told us, on the authority of Hushaym, who said: I am Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, who said: A woman came to Al-Numan bin Bashir, and she said: Her husband had intercourse with her maid, and Al-Numan said: But I have satisfactory news about that, which I narrate on the authority of the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “If you permit him, I will strike him one hundred times, and if you do not permit him, I will stone him.”"
"5362","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Bahrani told me, he said: Habban told us, meaning Ibn Hilal, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada was asked “about a man who had intercourse with a female slave.” His wife, and it was narrated while we were sitting, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, on the authority of Habib bin Yassaf, that it was reported to Al-Numan bin Bashir, and he said: “ I will judge it according to the judgment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. If it is lawful for him, I will lash him with a hundred lashes, and if it is not lawful for him. \I stoned him\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5363","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Hibban told us, he said: Aban told us, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Arfata, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that a man called: Abd al-Rahman bin Hunayn would go to Qarqura. That he had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl, so it was brought to Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, and he said: “I will judge her according to the case of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. If she made it permissible for you, I will flog you a hundred times, and if she did not make it permissible for you, I will stone you with stones.” So she said: “I made it permissible for him,” so he was flogged. One hundred.” Qatada said: So I wrote to Habib bin Salim, and he wrote to me about this. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5364","Abu Dawud told us, he said: A`rim told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Habib Bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Concerning a man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl: If she She made it lawful for him, flog him with a hundred lashes, and if she did not make it lawful for him, then stone him.”"
"5365","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Harith, On the authority of Salamah bin Al-Muhabbiq, he said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ruled regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife’s slave girl: If he forced her, then she is free. And according to him, she gets the same for her mistress, and if she obeys him, then she is his, and according to him, she gets the same for her mistress.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5366","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Salamah ibn Al-Mubaqq, “A man cheated on his wife’s slave girl, so that matter was reported to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: If he forced her, then she is free from his money, and he is obligated to share with her mistress, and if she was obedient to him, then she is free from his money, and the same is hers. \His money\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5367","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Hammad told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, “that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf “had a saffron covering over him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Is it immoral? He said: I married a woman. He said: What did you say the truth? He said: The weight of a stone of gold. He said: I have a sheep, even if it is a sheep."
"5368","Qutaibah told us, he said: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “saw Ali Abdul Rahman blew a whistle and said: What is this? He said: I married a woman worth the weight of a stone of gold. He said: May God bless you. “I have no sex, even with a sheep.”"
"5369","Ahmad bin Yahya bin Al-Wazir bin Suleiman told me, he said: Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr told us, he said: Suleiman bin Bilal told us, On the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Humaid al-Tawil, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw the opinion of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf He picked up a whistle and said: What is the matter? He said: I married a woman from the Ansar. He said: Do I know even a sheep?"
"5370","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, told us on the authority of Ash’ath, who is the son of Abdul-Malik Abu Hani, on the authority of Al-Hasan He said: Aqeel bin Abi Talib married his wife from Bani Jathm, and he was told: With prosperity and children. He said: Say as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. May God bless him and grant him peace: May God bless you and bless you. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5371","Mujahid bin Musa al-Baghdadi told us, saying: Hushaym, meaning Ibn Bashir al-Wasiti, told us on the authority of Abu Balj, and his name is Yahya bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hatib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Separating what is permissible from what is forbidden, the tambourine and the sound in marriage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5372","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Khaled bin Dhakwan told us, on the authority of al-Rabi’, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me.” He greeted me in the morning and sat on my bed, while our maidens were beating the tambourine and lamenting those who killed my fathers. One of them said: And we are dead. A prophet who knows what comes tomorrow, so he said to her: Keep quiet about this and say what you were saying before.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5373","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Balaj, he said: I heard Muhammad bin Hatib, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The difference between what is permissible and what is forbidden is the sound.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5374","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amir bin Saad, he said: I entered upon Qardha bin Ka’b, Abu Masoud Al-Ansari was at a wedding, and suddenly a group of people were singing, so I said: “You are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the people of Badr.” He will do this for you. They said: Sit down. If you wish, listen with us, and if you wish, go, for he has given us permission to have fun at the wedding. \""
5375"""
"5375","Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed us, saying: Ya'la narrated to us, saying: Al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: ""'A'ishah married a female relative of hers to a man of the Ansar. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Did you send the girl off? Why did you not send with her someone who would say: ""We have come to you, we have come to you; may we live long and may you live long?""'"""
"5376","'Amr ibn Mansur al-Nasa'i informed us, saying: Hisham ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that 'Ali said: ""I married Fatimah (ra), so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, consummate the marriage for me.' He said: 'Give her something.' I said: 'I have nothing.' He said: 'Where is your Hutami shield?' I said: 'It is with me.' He said: 'Give it to her.'"" Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah contradicted him."
"5377","Harun bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Sa`id, meaning Ibn Abi Orouba, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: “When Ali, may God be pleased with him, married Fatima, may God be pleased with her, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Give her something. He said: I have nothing. He said: Where is your Hatamiyah shield?"
"5378","Muhammad ibn Adam told us, on the authority of Abdah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me.” He greeted me when I was six years old, and he came in to me when I was nine years old, and I was playing with the girls.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5379","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, and Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, He said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Aisha when she was six or seven years old, and she was married to him when she was nine years old, and he played with her.” He lived with her, and he died on her behalf when she was eighteen years old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5380","Ahmad bin Saad bin Al-Hakam bin Abi Maryam told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Amara told me Ibn Ghaziyah, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah Ibn Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me.” Peace be upon him, when she was six years old, and he built a marriage with her when she was nine years old. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5381","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Waki` told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Urwa, on the authority of his father Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me in Shawwal, and he married me in Shawwal, so which of his wives was more fortunate with him than me?"
"5382","Nusayr bin Al-Faraj Al-Tarsusi told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prepared Fatima in a khamil, a skin-skin, and a human pillow stuffed with Idhkhir.”"
"5383","Muhammad ibn Salamah and Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala informed us. He said: Ibn Wahb informed us. He said: Abu Hani al-Khawlani informed me. He heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubli saying: On the authority of Jabir bin Abd Allah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “A bed “A bed for a man, a bed for his wife, a third for a guest, and a fourth for the devil.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5384","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me He said: “Have you gotten married, Jabir?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Did you adopt patterns? I said: Then he mentioned a word that means: And how? Do we have patterns? He said: “It will be.”"
"5385","Ziyad bin Ayyub told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “He invaded Khaybar, and we then prayed the morning prayer in a group of people. Then the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rode, and Abu Talha rode. I was a companion of Abu Talha, and he took the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the horizon of Khaybar, and I could see the white of the thigh of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. When he entered the village, he said: God is Great, Khaybar has been destroyed. When we camped in a people’s square, the morning of those who had been warned would be bad. He said it three times. Several times, he said: And the people went out to their work. Abdul Aziz said: They said: Muhammad. Abdul Aziz said: And some of our companions said: And on Thursday, we attacked her by force, and the captives were gathered. Dihya came and said: O Prophet of God, give me a slave girl from the captivity. He said: Go. So take a maid, so he took Safiya bint Huyay, and a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Prophet of God, you gave Dihya Safiyya bint Huyayy, the lady of Qurayza, and al-Nadir, it is only suitable for you. He said: So call him for it. So he brought it, and when the Prophet looked at it, he prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Take another slave girl from captivity. He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, freed her and married her, even if On the way, Umm Sulaim prepared it for him and gave it to him during the night, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, became a bride. He said: Who was He has something, let him bring it. He said: He spread out Nata’, and the man made the man bring the aqat, and he made the man bring the dates, and he made the man bring the ghee. They felt anxious, and it was the feast of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5386","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulayman told us, he said: Abu Bakr told me, on the authority of Sulayman, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Humaid, He heard Anas say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “stayed with Safiyya bint Huyyay bin Akhtab on the road to Khaybar for three days.” When he proposed to her, then she was among those over whom the veil was imposed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5387","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Abi Al-Mawwal told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He teaches us istikharah in all matters just as he teaches us a surah from the Qur’an. He says: If one of you is concerned about a matter... Let him perform two rak'ahs other than the obligatory prayer, then say: O God, I seek guidance from You with Your knowledge, I seek Your help with Your power, and I ask You from Your great grace, for You have power and I do not have power, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. Oh God, if You know that this matter is good. For me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affairs, or he said: In my immediate and future affairs, so ordain it for me and make it easy for me, then bless me in it, even if you You know that this matter is bad for me in my religion, my livelihood, and the outcome of my affairs, or he said: In my immediate and future affairs, so turn it away from me, and turn me away from it. “And ordain for me what is good wherever it may be, then please me with it.” He said: “And he names his need.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5388","Ubayd Allah bin Sa`id Abu Qudamah al-Sarkhasi informed us, saying: Yahya told us, he is the son of Sa`id al-Qattan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, he is the son of Omar, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah, who is the son of Omar, “that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a fatwa.” peace be upon him, and he said: Abdullah divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so he said: Order Abdullah to take her back, then leave her until she is cleansed of This menstruation of hers, then she will menstruate another menstruation, and when she becomes pure, then if he wishes, he may separate from her before he has intercourse with her, and if he wishes So let him keep her, for it is the waiting period for which God Almighty has commanded that women should be divorced.”"
"5389","Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Masry informed us, saying: Ibn Al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “He divorced His wife was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello to that, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Tell him to take her back, then to keep her until she is pure, then she will menstruate, then If he wishes, he may retain it after that, and if he wishes, he may divorce him before he has touched it. That is the waiting period with which God Almighty has commanded that women should be divorced.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5390","Kathir bin Ubaid Al-Humsi told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Harb, he said: Al-Zubaidi told us, and his name is Muhammad bin Al-Walid, he said: Al-Zuhri was asked: How? Divorce due to waiting period? He said: Salem told me that Abdullah bin Omar said: I divorced my wife during the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was menstruating. He mentioned That was the lifetime of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, became angry about that, so he said: “Let him review it, then He keeps her until she has menstruated and becomes pure. If it seems to him that he should divorce her in a pure state before touching her, then that divorce is for the waiting period as God has commanded. Almighty, “Abdullah bin Omar said, “So I took her back, and the divorce that I divorced him was counted for her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5391","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Tamim told me on the authority of Hajjaj. Ibn Juraij said: Abu Al-Zubayr, that he heard Abd al-Rahman bin Ayman asking Ibn Omar, and Abu al-Zubayr was listening, so he said: “What do you think of a man who divorces his menstruating wife? He said to him: Abdullah bin Omar divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So Omar asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, and he said: “Abdullah bin Omar divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: To take her back, so he returned her to me.” He said: When she is pure, let him divorce her or keep her. Ibn Omar said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Prophet, when you divorce women. So divorce them before their waiting period.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5392","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I heard a mujahid telling him, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “In His saying, the Almighty the Majestic: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them according to their waiting period.” Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, said: It was accepted \Their 'iddah\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5393","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub al-Marwazi told us, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, said: “Divorce according to the Sunnah is that he divorces her once while she is pure without intercourse, then if she menstruates and is pure.” He divorced her with another woman, and when she menstruated and became pure, he divorced her again, then she went through the waiting period after that after her menstruation.” Al-A’mash said: I asked Abraham, and he said Like that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5394","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, he is Al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, On the authority of Abdullah, he said: “Divorce according to the Sunnah is that he divorces her in a pure state without intercourse.”"
"5395","Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he is Ibn Sulaiman, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so Omar went and informed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “Come by Abdullah and let him see her, and when she has bathed, then let him leave her until she has menstruated, and when she has washed From her last menstrual period, he should not touch her until he divorces her. If he wants to keep her, let him keep her, for it is the waiting period that God has commanded. “Glory be to Him, that women may be divorced for her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5396","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan is Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman. Mawla Talha, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, “He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so he mentioned that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted him and said: “Tell him to have intercourse with her, then to divorce her while she is pure or pregnant.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5397","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told me, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar. “He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned her to him, until he divorced her while she was pure.”"
"5398","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, he said: I asked Ibn Omar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he said: Do you know Abdullah bin Omar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. So Omar asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered him to take her back. I said: Should she observe that divorce? He said: What do you think if he is unable? And he took a bath? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5399","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Yunus, he is Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Yunus Ibn Jubayr, he said: I said to Ibn Omar, “A man divorced his wife while she was menstruating.” He said: Do you know Abdullah bin Omar? He divorced his wife. She was menstruating, so Omar came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, asking him, so he ordered him to check with her, then she would receive her waiting period. I said to him: So A man divorced his wife while she was menstruating. Is that divorce considered a waiting period? He said: “What if he is unable and has become a woman?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5400","Suleiman bin Dawud Abu Rabi’ told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, Makhramah told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Mahmoud bin Labid, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed about a man who divorced his wife three times in total. He got up angry, then said: Is he playing? With the Book of God while I was among you, until a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, shall I not kill him? Abu Abd al-Rahman said: I do not know anyone? He narrated this hadith without a trace."
"5401","Muhammad bin Salamah Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, that Sahl Ibn Saad Al-Saadi told him, “Uwaimira Al-Ijli came to Asim Ibn Adi and said: Have you seen, O Asim, if a man was found with his wife? A man. Should he kill him and they should kill him? Or how should he do it? Ask me, O Asim, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about that. So Asim asked the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, disliked the issues and criticized them, to the point that what he heard from the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was difficult for Asim. May God bless him and grant him peace. When Asim returned to his family, Uwaimir came to him and said: O Asim, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say to you? Asim said to Uwaimir: You did not bring me anything good. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked the question that you asked about. Uwaimir said: By God, I will not finish until I ask the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it. So Uwaimir approached until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came in the middle of People, and he said: O Messenger of God, “Have you seen a man who found a man with his wife? Should he kill him and you would kill him?” Or how does he do it? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It was revealed about you and your companion, so go and bring her. Sahl said: So we will meet, and I will be with the people. With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he finished, Uwaimir said, he said: I lied to her, O Messenger of God, if I caught her. So he divorced her three times. Before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5402","Ahmad bin Yahya Al-Sufi Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym, whose name is Al-Fadl bin Dukayn, told us, he said: Sa’id bin Yazid told us. Al-Ahmasi, he said: Al-Sha’bi told us, he said: Fatima bint Qais told me, she said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I am the daughter of Al Khaled, and my husband so-and-so sent me a message to divorce me, and I asked his family for maintenance and housing, but they refused me. They said: O Messenger of God, he He sent to her with three divorces. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The maintenance and housing are for the woman, if she She is obligated to take her back to her husband.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5403","Muhammad bin Bashar Bandar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he is Ibn Mahdi, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Salamah That is, Ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The woman who has been divorced three times has neither residence nor \expense\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5404","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Dinar Al-Humsi told us, saying: Baqiyya, he is Ibn Al-Walid, told us, on the authority of Abu Amr He is Al-Awza’i. He said: Yahya told us. He is Ibn Abi Kathir. He said: Abu Salamah told me. He is Ibn Abd al-Rahman. He said: You told me. Fatima bint Qais, that Amr bin Hafs Al-Makhzoumi divorced her three times, so Khalid bin Al-Walid set off with a group of Banu Makhzum to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, Abu Amr bin Hafs: “He divorced Fatima three times. Is she entitled to maintenance?” So the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him: “She has no maintenance or accommodation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5405","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Abu Asim, who is the nobleman, told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of His father, that Abu Al-Sahba came to Ibn Abbas and said: O Ibn Abbas, “Did you not know that the three were during the era of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? May God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, and those who came from the caliphate of Omar, may God be pleased with them, are they returned to one? He said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5406","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked “about a man who divorced his wife, so she married another husband and he had intercourse with her, then He divorced her before he had intercourse with her. Is it permissible for the first one? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No, until the other one tastes her honey, and she tastes it. \His sweetheart\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5407","Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told me, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ayoub bin Musa told me, On the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The woman of Rifa’ah al-Qurazi came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, I had intercourse with Abd al-Rahman bin al-Zubayr, and by God, he only has a gift like this. So the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Perhaps you want to return to Rifa’ah, so that he may taste your honey and you may taste his honey?"
"5408","Amr bin Ali Abu Hafs told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The wife of Rifa’ah Al-Qurazi came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while Abu Bakr was with him, and she said: O Messenger of God, I was under the guardianship of Al-Qurazi, and he divorced me outright, so I married Abd al-Rahman bin al-Zubayr. By God, O Messenger of God, he did not He had only one such scarf, and she took a scarf from her robe, and Khaled bin Saeed was at the door, but he was not allowed to enter, so he said: O Abu Bakr, do you not hear this woman speaking out loudly in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: You want to return to Rifa’ah? No, until you taste his honey and he tastes yours.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5409","Ali bin Nasr bin Ali Al-Jahdhami Basri told us, he said: Suleiman bin Harb told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: I said To Ayoub: “Have you known anyone who said regarding your affairs in your hand: There are three things, other than the good ones?” And he said: No, then he said: O God, forgive, except for what Qatada told me, On the authority of Kathir, the freed slave of Ibn Samurah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Three,” so I met many, So I asked him but he did not recognize it, so I returned to Qatada and told him, and he said: He forgot. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5410","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She came The wife of Rifaat al-Qurti went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “My husband divorced me, but he refused to divorce me, and I married after him.” Abd al-Rahman bin al-Zubayr, and he had nothing but something like this garment. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed and said: Perhaps you want to “Do you return to Rifa’ah, so that he may taste your honey, and you may taste his honey?”"
"5411","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, he is Al-Qattan, he said: Ubayd Allah told me, meaning Ibn Umar, he said: Al-Qasim told me, he Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, “A man divorced his wife three times, so she married a man, and he divorced her before he touched her. The Messenger of God was asked: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Is it permissible for the first one? He said: No, so that he may taste its sweetness as the first one tasted. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5412","Ali bin Hajar Al-Maruzi informed us, he said: Hushaym informed us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, “Al-Ghumaysa’a or Al-Rumaysa’a came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, complaining to her husband that he was not having access to her. It was not long before her husband came and said: O Messenger of God, she is lying, and he is reaching for her, but she wants to return to Her first husband, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Not until you taste his honey. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5413","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, he said: I heard Salim bin Razin narrates, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In a man there is He has a woman whom he divorces, then another man marries her, and he divorces her before he has intercourse with her, so she returns to her first husband. He said: No. Until you taste the honey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5414","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Marthad, on the authority of Razin bin Suleiman Al-Ahmari, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked “about a man who divorces his wife three times, then the man marries her and closes his marriage.” He opened the door and lowered the curtain, then divorced her before he entered with her. He said: “It is not permissible for the first one until the other has intercourse with her.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is more correct than the one before it, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5415","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzail, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the one who tattoos and the one who was tattooed, the one who is connected to her and the one connected to her, and the one who consumes usury.” And his client, and the one who makes it lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful.”"
"5416","Al-Hussein bin Harith told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: I asked Al-Zuhri about the woman who sought refuge from The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha: “When the Kalabiyya entered upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, She said: I seek refuge in God from you. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You have sought refuge with a great sin. Take care of your family. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5417","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed Abu Qudamah Al-Sarkhasi told us, saying: Abdul Rahman, he is Ibn Mahdi, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he is Al-Thawri, On the authority of Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Abi Al-Jahm, he said: I heard Fatima bint Qays saying: “My husband sent me a divorce letter, so I tightened my clothes, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: How many divorces did he divorce you? I said: Three. He said: You are not entitled to maintenance, and perform the waiting period in the house of your paternal uncle Ibn Umm Maktum. He is one who is blind. You throw away your clothes with him. When your waiting period is over, then inform me.” Mukhtasar, Ubayd Allah ibn Sa’id told us, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tamim, servant of Fatima, on the authority of Fatima, and the like. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5418","Abdullah bin Abdul-Samad bin Ali Al-Mawsili informed us, saying: Mukhlid, he is the son of Yazid, told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he is Al-Thawri, on the authority of Salem is the snub-nosed bin Ajlan, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to him and said: “I have made my wife forbidden to me.” He said: You lied, it is not forbidden to you. Then he recited this verse: O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you? You have to pay the severity of the expiation. \free a slave\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5419","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he heard Ubaid, meaning bin Umair al-Laythi, he said: I heard Aisha The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stay with Zainab and drink honey from her, so Hafsa and I made peace. O one of us, whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, enters upon her, let her say: “Indeed, I smell a pleasant scent from you.” So he entered upon one of them, and she said that to him, and he said: Rather, I drank honey at Zainab’s house, and he said: I will not do it again, so he descended: O Prophet, why do you forbid what God has made lawful for you? If you repent to God To Aisha and Hafsa: I did not understand Hafsa as I wanted, and when the Prophet confided to some of his wives that he said: “Rather, I drank honey,” this The whole speech is in the hadith of Ataa. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith has a very good and authentic chain of narration. This hadith of Aisha is about honey. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5420","Muhammad bin Hatim bin Nu’aym told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning Ibn Makki Ibn Isa, he said: Abdullah, he is Ibn al-Mubarak, told us, He said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, he said: I heard Ka’b bin Malik, narrating His speech when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, and he said in it: When the Messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He comes to me and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you. Abu al-Rabi’ Sulayman ibn Dawud informed me. He said: Ibn Dawud informed us. Wahb, on the authority of Yunus, Ibn Shihab said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik informed me that Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik, he said: I heard Ka'b bin Malik narrating his story when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, and he related his story. And he said: “Until forty had passed, then a messenger from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He commands you to separate from your wife. So I said: Should I divorce her or what? He said: No, rather, separate from her and do not approach her. So I said to my wife: Have the right to do so? With your family, stay with them until God Almighty decides this matter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5421","Muhammad ibn Jablah al-Rafiqi and Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Harrani told me, saying: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayn told us, he said: He told us My father, on the authority of Ishaq bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b bin Malik told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Abu Ka’b bin Malik, one of the three who repented, speaking: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to me, and to My companion, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to keep away from your wives, so I said to his Messenger: Should I divorce my wife or what should I do? He said: No, but keep away from her and do not approach her. So I said to my wife: Go to your family and be among them, so she joined them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5422","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: Aqeel told me On the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b told me that Abdullah bin Ka’b said: I heard Ka’b narrating His speech when he lagged behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, and he said in it: “Behold, a messenger of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He comes to me and says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commands you to separate from your wife. So I said: Should I divorce her or what should I do? He said: Rather, stay away from her and do not approach her, and he sent something similar to my companion, so I said to my wife: Go with your family and be with them, until May God Almighty decide this matter.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ma’qil ibn Ubayd Allah disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5423","Muhammad bin Ma’dan bin Isa bin Ma’dan Al-Harrani told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Ma’qil told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, He said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abdullah bin Ka’b told me, on the authority of his uncle Ubaid Allah bin Ka’b, who said: I heard Abu Ka’b bin Malik, who is one of the He spoke of the three upon whom he repented. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to me and to my companions that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent He commanded you to keep away from your wives. I said to the Messenger: Should I divorce her or what should I do? He said: No, but keep her away from her and do not approach her. So I said to my wife? “Go with your family, and stay with them until God Almighty decrees.” So I joined them. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Mu’mar disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5424","5468 Muhammad Ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani informed me, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Thawr, informed us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, said in his hadith: “When a messenger from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to me, he said: Retire. Your wife, so I said: Should I divorce her? He said: No, but do not approach her. He did not mention in it: Join your family. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5425","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I heard Yahya, who is the son of Sa’id al-Qattan, he said: Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yahya told us Ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Omar Ibn Utab, that Abu Hassan, the client of Banu Nawfal, told him, saying: “My wife and I were mamluks. So I divorced her twice, then we were both emancipated. So I asked Ibn Abbas, and he said: If you take her back, you have only one wife. He decided that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"5426","5470 Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, saying: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Omar bin Mu’tab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the client of Banu Nawfal, said: Ibn Abbas was asked “about a slave who divorced his wife twice, then both were freed.” Should he marry her? He said: Yes. He said: From whom? He said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, give a fatwa about that? Abdul Razzaq said: Ibn al-Razzaq said: Al-Mubarak to Muammar: Who is this Hassan? He carried a great rock (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5427","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman, the companion of Al-Shafi’i, told us: Asad bin Musa told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khutmi, On the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, on the authority of Kathir bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: Ibn Qurayzah told me, “They presented it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. On the day of Qurayza, whoever had a wet dream or whose pubic hair had grown will be killed, and whoever had not had a wet dream or whose pubic hair had not grown will be left behind.”"
"5428","Muhammad ibn Mansour al-Makki informed us, saying: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Atiya al-Qurazi, he said: “I was “The day Sa’d ruled over Banu Qurayza as a young man, they became suspicious of me and did not find me to show up, so I was left behind, so here I am before you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5429","Abu Qudamah Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Umar, he said: He informed me Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “came to see him on the day of Uhud, when he was fourteen years old, but it was not permissible for him.” He came to him on the day of the ditch, when he was fifteen years old, and he granted him permission.”"
"5430","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Pen was lifted from three people: from the sleeper until he wakes up, And on behalf of a child until he grows up, and on behalf of an insane person until he regains his senses or regains his senses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5431","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi and Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told us, saying: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God Almighty has overlooked from my nation everything that I have narrated.” themselves, unless they speak or act.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5432","Abdullah bin Saeed Abu Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God has transcended for my nation what they have whispered about and talked about within themselves, unless act or speak with it.”"
"5433","Musa bin Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi al-Kufi told me, saying: Husayn al-Ja’fi told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Shayban, meaning Ibn Abd. Al-Rahman Al-Nahwi, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Indeed, God Almighty “It goes beyond what my nation has ever told itself, unless it is spoken of or acted upon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5434","Abu Bakr bin Nafi’ told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a Persian neighbor who was very kind. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day and was with him. Aisha, so he motioned to him with his hand to come, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, motioned to Aisha, meaning: and this one, Then the other one gestured to him like this with his hand: “No,” two or three times."
"5435","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Maslamah told us, he is Al-Qanabi, he said: Malik and Al-Harith bin told us. Poor person. I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, On the authority of Alqamah bin Waqqas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, and in the hadith of Al-Harith that he heard Omar say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Actions are by intention, and a person is only by what he intended. So whoever’s emigration is to God and His Messenger, his emigration is to God.” And His Messenger, and whoever’s emigration was for the sake of this world or a woman to marry, his emigration was for the sake of what he emigrated to.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5436","Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid Al-Homsi told us, he said: Ali bin Ayyash told us, he said: Shuaib, the son of Abi Hamza, told me, And Abu Hamza’s name is Dinar. He said: Abu al-Zinad told me, from what Abd al-Rahman al-Araj told him, from what he mentioned, that he heard Abu Hurairah He tells him, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: And he said: “Look how God turns away from me the cursing of the Quraysh and curses them. They are cursing reprehensible, and they curse reprehensible, and I am Muhammad.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5437","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid and Musa bin Ali informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the Messenger of God was commanded May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to choose his wives. He started with me and said: I have mentioned a matter to you, so you should not be in a hurry until you consult your parents. She said: He knew that my parents would not order me to separate from him. She said: Then he recited this verse: O Prophet, tell your wives if you You want the life of this world and its adornments to His saying: Beautiful. So I said: What of this should I consult with my parents, for I want God Almighty. And His Messenger and the Hereafter. Aisha said: Then the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did the same as I did, and that did not happen at that time. He said They divorced the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they chose to divorce him because they chose him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5438","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Thawr told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “When it was revealed, ‘And if you were desiring God and His Messenger and the Hereafter, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me and began to He said: O Aisha, I am mentioning a matter to you, so do not be in a hurry until you ask your parents for advice. She said: By God, he knows that my parents They would not have ordered me to separate from him, so he recited to me: O Prophet, tell your wives, if you desire the life of this world and its adornments, then come. So I said: Is this what I ask for advice from my parents, for I want God and His Messenger and the Hereafter. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake, and the first is more likely to be correct, and the hadith of Yunus, and Musa bin Ali, who was before him, is more likely to be correct. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5439","5483 Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya, he is Al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Ismail, he is Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a choice, so we chose him. Was that a divorce?”"
"5440","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana’ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim, he said: Al-Shu’abi said, on the authority of Masruq On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a choice to his wives, but it was not a divorce.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5441","Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Sadran Basri told us, Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a choice to his wives, but it was not a divorce.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5442","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a choice to his wives. Was it a divorce?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5443","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Da’eef told me, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a choice, so we chose him, but he did not promise us anything.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5444","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Hammad bin Masada told us, he said: Ibn Mawhib told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: Aisha had a boy and a slave girl, she said: “I wanted to free them, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Start with the boy before the girl. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5445","Muhammad bin Salamah Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Al-Qasim informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Rabi’ah, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There were three Sunnahs in Birah, and one of the three Sunnahs was that she was freed, so she was given the choice of Her husband, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Loyalty goes to the one who is freed. And the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered, and the tinder is pouring. With meat, so bread was brought to him, and a human being from the human family, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have I not seen a twine with meat in it? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, but that is meat that you give in charity to Bareerah, and you do not eat charity. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “It is a charity due on her, a gift for us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
